00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.830 align:start position:0%
a ukrainian tank fires down a street  almost completely destroyed  soldiers take cover underground as what  sounds like an artillery shell explodes  close by these men are defending the  last areas of severe donetsk still under  their control from the slow russian  advance  ammunition and supplies are ferried  across the river from neighbouring  lesichansk the four bridges that  connected them are destroyed  fighting has been intense here for weeks  because these are the only two cities in  the lugansk region that russia hasn't  taken ukrainian reinforcements head to  the front line many of these men had  never held a gun before the war started  and they come from all walks of life the  government says hundreds of ukrainian  soldiers are being killed every day  there is little verifiable information  on how many russians are dying  the situation on the front line hasn't  significantly changed thanks to tactical  maneuvers the ukrainian army is  strengthening its defense of the luhansk  region that is really the toughest spot  the occupiers are pressing strongly and  also in the dynastic direction in the  kharkiv region  this video was supplied to the reuters  news agency by russian forces it  reportedly shows pro-russia separatists  advancing on ukrainian positions near  civil dynetsk the fighter shows western  supplied military hardware including an  anti-tank system night vision equipment  and rifles that he says were abandoned  by retreating ukrainian forces he says  the blurred out bodies are ukrainian  soldiers  we will continue to make inroads into  their lines to fully surround them i  think if they're not idiots they will  surrender if they don't want to  surrender they will die  the ukrainian army says russian forces  have cut supply routes from two villages  south of lusichansk and several donetsk  the head of lugansk military  administration confirms that claim  and says that russian forces have taken  control of another three villages in the  same area there are also reports that  russian forces are advancing close to  the azot chemical plant inside several  donetsk  where it's understood that hundreds of  civilians including women and children  are sheltering inside charles stratford  al jazeera kiev
 

